Round 19 (2026-02-27)

What landed
- Files changed:
  - `clang/aot/_.c`
  - `clang/heap/alloc.c`
  - `clang/runtime/eval_main.c`
- Goal of this round: attribute global heap allocation traffic caused during compiled execution, not just explicit `aot_alloc(...)` sites.

Runtime/instrumentation changes
1) Added global compiled-context heap attribution (`HVM_AOT_HEAP_ATTR`):
- New TLS compiled-depth marker:
  - `AOT_HEAP_COMPILED_DEPTH`
  - entered/exited in both compiled dispatch paths:
    - `aot_call_ref(...)`
    - `aot_try_call(...)`
- New accounting hook in allocator boundary:
  - `heap_alloc(...)` now calls `aot_heap_alloc_note(size)` after successful allocation.
- New counters in `aot/_.c`:
  - `AOT_HEAP total_calls/total_nodes`
  - size histogram buckets:
    - `1`, `2`, `3`, `4`, `5`, `6`, `7`, `8`, `9-16`, `17+`
- New dump path in runtime:
  - `runtime_eval_main(...)` now prints `aot_heap_attr_dump(stderr)`.

2) Existing explicit AOT site telemetry remains unchanged:
- `HVM_AOT_ALLOC` still reports only explicit emitted/wrapper classes (`APP_FRAME_*`, `DUP_CELL`, `CTR_FIELDS`, `ENV_BIND`).
- New `AOT_HEAP` complements it by covering all `heap_alloc` during compiled context.

Why this matters
- It resolves the major observability gap: previous `AOT_ALLOC` undercounted real heap traffic (especially `edit_dist`) because most allocations came from generic runtime constructors/helpers invoked while compiled code was active.

