Important observations
- `AOT_HEAP` is now very close to total runtime heap on canaries (difference is tiny), proving most heap traffic is generated while executing compiled code paths, not only at explicit `aot_alloc` sites.
- `edit_dist` gap is explained: not an attribution bug anymore; the compiled path itself is allocating heavily through generic constructors/helpers (`size=1/2` dominated histogram).
- Remaining performance work should prioritize reducing expression-level term materialization (especially repeated size-2 node allocation patterns), not further micro-optimizing only explicit `DUP_CELL` counters.
- `env_locs[idx] == 0` sentinel remains safe with current allocator initialization (`heap_init_slices`: thread 0 starts at 1).

